---
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Keesing Puzzle Hunt"
  description="Privacy policy for the Keesing Puzzle Hunt SMS service."
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <article class="policy-page site-container">
      <header class="policy-header">
        <h1>Privacy Policy — Keesing Puzzle Hunt</h1>
        <p class="last-updated"><strong>Last updated: October 8, 2026</strong></p>
      </header>

      <div class="policy-content">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes how information is handled when you
          participate in the Keesing Puzzle Hunt SMS service (“the Hunt”).
        </p>

        <p>
          The Hunt is designed to collect and retain as little personal
          information as possible.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We Receive</h2>

        <p>
          When you communicate with the Hunt by text message, the service may
          receive:
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Your phone number.</strong> Your phone number is used to identify
          your participation, maintain your current game state, and send
          responses to your messages.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Messages you send.</strong> This includes commands such as JOIN,
          HELP, and STOP and location links that you choose to send as part of
          the Hunt.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Location information you explicitly send.</strong> Some Hunt
          activities ask you to share your current location by sending a
          location link from your phone. The service extracts the latitude and
          longitude contained in that message in order to calculate your
          distance from a Hunt target.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Hunt does <strong>not</strong> continuously track your location and
          cannot access your location unless you explicitly send it.
        </p>

        <h2>How Location Information Is Used</h2>

        <p>
          When you send a location, the service calculates your distance from
          the Hunt target so that it can provide clues such as WARMER or COLDER.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Hunt is designed <strong>not to store the latitude or longitude you
          send</strong>. Instead, after calculating your distance from the target,
          the service retains only the previous calculated distance needed to
          determine whether your next location is warmer or colder.
        </p>

        <p>Your location history is not maintained by the Hunt.</p>

        <h2>Information We Store</h2>

        <p>
          The Hunt stores only the information needed to operate the game. This
          may include:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Your phone number;</li>
          <li>Whether you have joined the Hunt; and</li>
          <li>Your most recently calculated distance from the current target.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          The system is designed to minimize retention of personal information.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you text <strong>STOP</strong>, the Hunt deletes the game state
          associated with your phone number and stops sending Hunt responses,
          subject to any records that telecommunications or infrastructure
          providers are independently required to maintain.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>

        <p>Information received through the Hunt is used only to:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Operate the Hunt;</li>
          <li>Respond to your messages;</li>
          <li>Determine your progress in location-based Hunt activities;</li>
          <li>Maintain your participation and opt-in/opt-out status; and</li>
          <li>Diagnose technical problems and maintain the service.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Participant information is not used for advertising or marketing.</p>

        <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>

        <p>
          We do <strong>not sell, rent, or share participant information with third
          parties for advertising, marketing, data brokerage, or other unrelated
          purposes.</strong>
        </p>

        <p>
          The Hunt uses service providers, including telecommunications and
          internet infrastructure providers, to transmit messages and operate
          the service. These providers necessarily process some information in
          order to provide their services.
        </p>

        <p>
          For example, an SMS provider must process your phone number and
          messages in order to deliver them, and an internet hosting provider
          processes network requests required to operate the Hunt.
        </p>

        <p>Information may also be disclosed if required by law.</p>

        <h2>SMS Communications</h2>

        <p>Participation is voluntary. You may text <strong>JOIN</strong> to participate.</p>

        <p>
          Message frequency varies depending on how often you interact with the
          Hunt. Message and data rates may apply.
        </p>

        <p>Text <strong>HELP</strong> for instructions or assistance.</p>

        <p>
          Text <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to stop receiving Hunt messages.
          You may need to text <strong>START</strong> if you later wish to re-enable
          SMS messages.
        </p>

        <h2>Security and Data Minimization</h2>

        <p>The Hunt is designed around data minimization. In particular:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>It does not continuously track participants;</li>
          <li>Location is provided only when a participant explicitly sends it;</li>
          <li>The Hunt does not retain a history of submitted locations;</li>
          <li>
            Submitted latitude and longitude are not stored as participant game
            state; and
          </li>
          <li>
            Only the minimum state needed to provide the Hunt experience is
            retained.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Reasonable technical measures are used to protect the information
          processed by the service.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          The Hunt may be played by families, but the SMS service is not intended
          to collect personal information from children independently. Children
          should participate using a parent or guardian's phone and with their
          supervision.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

        <p>
          This policy may be updated if the Hunt or the technologies used to
          provide it change. The current version will be posted on this page.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          Questions about this Privacy Policy or the Hunt can be directed to:
        </p>

        <address>
          <strong>Ron Keesing</strong><br />
          <strong><a href="mailto:ron@keesingai.com">ron@keesingai.com</a></strong>
        </address>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .policy-page {
    max-width: 920px;
    padding-top: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(5rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .policy-header {
    padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .policy-header h1 {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.25rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .last-updated {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .policy-content {
    max-width: 780px;
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.35vw, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .policy-content h2 {
    margin: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.75rem) 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .policy-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .policy-content ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
  }

  .policy-content li + li {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .policy-content strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .policy-content address {
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .policy-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2rem;
  }

  .policy-content a:hover,
  .policy-content a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
